    "rationale": "Task-exchangeability for ∆̂_j is most defensible within tier (same target type, same wording template). Crossing tiers requires arguing that the LLM's bias structure is invariant to (a) target — country vs. president vs. policy action vs. institution — and (b) wording — satisfied/dissatisfied vs. approve/disapprove vs. favorable/unfavorable. Pew's own toplines show systematic gaps across these tiers within the same field period, so cross-tier pooling is an LLM-bias claim, not a population-proportion claim."
  }
